   148→
   149→| Field | Description | Default |
   150→|-------|-------------|---------|
   151→| `devcontainer` | Explicit path to devcontainer.json | Auto-detected |
   152→| `extra_commands` | Additional commands to route to the container | `[]` |
   153→| `anonymous_volumes` | Container volumes (e.g., `node_modules`) | `["node_modules"]` |
   154→| `shared.files` | Files/directories to share across branch workspaces | `[]` |
   155→
   156→### `~/.dual/workspaces.toml` (global state)
   157→
   158→Managed by Dual. Tracks all registered workspaces.
   159→
   160→```toml
   161→workspace_root = "~/dual-workspaces"
   162→
   163→[[workspaces]]
   164→repo = "my-project"
   165→url = "git@github.com:org/my-project.git"
   166→branch = "main"
   167→path = "/Users/you/code/my-project"
   168→
   169→[[workspaces]]
   170→repo = "my-project"
   171→url = "git@github.com:org/my-project.git"
   172→branch = "feat/auth"
   173→```
   174→
   175→## How It Works
   176→
   177→When you select a workspace (via `dual` or `dual launch`):
   178→
   179→1. **Clone** — Clones the repo into `{workspace_root}/{repo}/{branch}/` (uses `git clone --local` from main workspace for speed)
   180→2. **Shared files** — Copies shared config files (`.env.local`, `.vercel`, etc.) from `~/.dual/shared/{repo}/`
   181→3. **Container** — Creates and starts a Docker container with the clone bind-mounted
   182→4. **Setup** — Runs `setup` command on first launch (e.g., `pnpm install`)
   183→5. **Shell RC** — Generates transparent command routing that intercepts runtime commands and routes them to the container via `docker exec`
   184→6. **Tmux** — Creates a tmux session in the workspace directory and attaches
   185→
   186→Your editor, git, and credentials stay on the host. The container handles all runtime processes. Claude Code never knows it's running inside a container.
   187→
   188→### Shell Hook (Pane Propagation)
   189→
   190→On first run, `dual` automatically appends a small snippet to your `~/.zshrc` or `~/.bashrc`:
   191→
   192→```bash
   193→# dual: shell interception (auto-generated)
   194→if [ -n "$DUAL_ACTIVE" ] && [ -n "$DUAL_RC_PATH" ] && [ -f "$DUAL_RC_PATH" ]; then
   195→    source "$DUAL_RC_PATH"
   196→fi
   197→```
   198→
   199→This ensures that when you split a pane (`Ctrl+b %`) or create a new window (`Ctrl+b c`) inside a Dual tmux session, the new shell automatically loads command interception. Without this, new panes would run commands on the host instead of in the container.
   200→
   201→The snippet is a no-op outside Dual sessions — it only activates when `DUAL_ACTIVE` is set (which Dual configures via `tmux set-environment`).
   202→
   203→## Architecture
   204→
   205→```
   206→Terminal
   207→├── State A: Dual TUI (ratatui)
   208→│   └── Select workspace → suspend TUI → launch pipeline → tmux attach
   209→└── State B: tmux session
   210→    └── Detach (Ctrl+b d) → resume TUI
   211→
   212→Host                          Container
   213→+--------------------------+  +--------------------------+
   214→| nvim, git, claude, ssh   |  | pnpm, node, python       |
   215→| file reads/writes        |  | curl localhost, tests    |
   216→| credentials, SSH keys    |  | port-binding processes   |
   217→+--------------------------+  +--------------------------+
   218→        |    bind mount    |
   219→        +------------------+
   220→
   221→Browser --> {repo}-{branch}.localhost:{port}
   222→        --> reverse proxy
   223→        --> container
   224→```
